      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Storing high volumes of flammable solvents in high-density racking significantly reduces the escape time and limits rapid venting of combustion gases, which can trigger thermal runaway in nearby liquid loads as heat feedback exceeds their activation temperatures. In such confined spaces, heavy vapor accumulation often leads to a delayed but explosive ignition due to poor dispersion, while the structural integrity of steel racks is compromised by thermal softening, potentially causing catastrophic collapse that entrains loads and accelerates fire spread. Accurate modeling of these coupled thermal and structural failures is critical for determining the cause of the Rotterdam incident and assessing full liability.",
